---
description: Tenant, delivery, persistence and queue safety
globs: backend/api/**,backend/public-api/**,backend/worker/**,backend/scheduler/**,packages/application/**,packages/persistence/**,packages/queue/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Read the relevant handoff chapter and executing route, not only a similarly named legacy handler.
Authenticate AND authorize workspace membership/permission for every query/mutation; tenant admins are not global platform admins.
Preserve immutable email/flow versions, consent evidence, protected suppression, provider IDs and historical route authority.
Persist supported feedback before acknowledgement; validate SNS topic/signature. Never trust event tags to select a tenant.
Use exclusive claims/ownership for external submissions and scheduled work. Intent dedupe alone is not exactly-once sending. Never blindly retry unknown SES submissions.
Use valid stable BullMQ IDs and test actual PG/Redis concurrency. Keep action types partitioned between workers.
Inspect SQL constraints as well as Prisma schema before migrations. Preserve unrelated changes and historical data.
Fail closed for production secret/config gaps; customer-safe errors with server-side correlation.
